    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0117" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d16-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-29">April 29, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Former Naval Person to President, Personal and Secret Number 291.</p>
                <p>It seems to me most necessary that we should all settle together now first <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Husky</hi> and exploitation thereof and secondly the
                    future of <hi rendition="#small-caps">Anakim</hi> in light of Burma campaign
                    experiences and shipping stringency. There are also a number of other burning
                    questions which you and I could with advantage bring up to date.</p>
                <p>I think I could manage to be with you by Tuesday 11th May. I would bring Wavell,
                    Peirse and Admiral Somerville as well as Pound, Brooke, Portal, Mountbatten and
                    Leathers. Please say whether you <pb facs="0118" n="16" xml:id="pg16"/> would
                    like this or whether you would prefer to send your people over here which of
                    course would be easier for us.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d16-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d16-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Washington by the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
